  "english": [
    "he <b>signaled</b> contemptuously <b>with his hand</b> and said: <b>If goat is better, let</b> it be <b>sacrificed as the daily offering.</b> The daily offering is a lamb, proving that its meat is preferable to that of a goat. <b>The king said: Since he</b> not only disagrees with me but <b>has no reverence</b> for <b>the monarchy,</b> as evident from his contempt, <b>sever his right</b> hand. <b>He gave a bribe and</b> the official <b>severed his left hand. The king heard</b> that Yissakhar had deceived him <b>and</b> had the official <b>sever his right hand</b> as well. <b>Rav Yosef said: Blessed is God Who took retribution [<i>mitarpesei</i>] from Yissakhar of Kfar Barkai in this world</b> and did not wait to punish him more severely in the next world. His punishment fit the crime; because he would not dirty his hands with sacrificial blood and was overzealous in keeping his hands clean, both his hands were severed.",
    "<b>Rav Ashi said: Yissakhar of Kfar Barkai did not study</b> the <b>Mishna</b> and was an ignoramus who did not know that this <i>halakha</i> is stated explicitly in the mishna. <b>As we learned</b> in a mishna: <b>Rabbi Shimon says: Lambs take precedence</b> over <b>goats in every place</b> they are mentioned in the Bible. I <b>might</b> have thought that this is <b>because it is a</b> more <b>select species.</b> Therefore, <b>the verse states: “If he brings a lamb as his offering”</b> (Leviticus 4:32). The Torah passage where bringing a lamb as a sin-offering is discussed appears after the passage describing the sin-offering of a goat. The inconsistent order <b>teaches that both</b> these animals <b>are equal. Ravina said:</b> Yissakhar did not <b>even read the Bible</b> properly, <b>as it is written: “If a lamb”</b> (Leviticus 4:32), <b>“if a goat”</b> (Leviticus 3:12), teaching: <b>If one wishes let him bring a lamb; if one wishes let him bring a goat.</b> There is no clear preference."
  ],
  "gemara": [
    {
      "right": "0px",
      "width": "655px",
      "text": "<span class=\"sentence\" id=\"0\" type=\"start\">&star;</span>אַחְוִי בִּידֵיהּ: אִי גַּדְיָא יָאֵי, יִסַּק לִתְמִידָא. אֲמַר מַלְכָּא: הוֹאִיל וְלָא הֲוֵי לֵיהּ",
      "segment_ids": [
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "0px",
      "width": "655px",
      "text": "אֵימְתָא דְמַלְכוּתָא, נִיפְסְקוּ לְיַמִּינֵיהּ. יְהַב שׁוֹחַד וּפַסְקֵיהּ לִשְׂמָאלֵיהּ. שְׁמַע",
      "segment_ids": [
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "0px",
      "width": "655px",
      "text": "מַלְכָּא וּפַסְקֵיהּ לְיַמִּינֵיהּ. אָמַר <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Rav Yosef I, third-generation Amora\" data-authority-id=\"1764\" data-full-name=\"Rav Yosef I\" data-name-he=\"רב יוסף בר חייא\">רַב יוֹסֵף</span>: בְּרִיךְ רַחֲמָנָא דְּאַשְׁקְלֵיהּ <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-tanna\" data-sage-type=\"tanna\" title=\"Yissakhar from the village, first-generation Tanna\" data-authority-id=\"1998\" data-full-name=\"Yissakhar from the village\" data-name-he=\"יששכר איש כפר ברקאי\" data-crossline-group=\"name-ref-crossline-58648\">לְיִשָּׂשׂכָר</span>",
      "segment_ids": [
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "0px",
      "width": "655px",
      "text": "<span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-tanna\" data-sage-type=\"tanna\" title=\"Yissakhar from the village, first-generation Tanna\" data-authority-id=\"1998\" data-full-name=\"Yissakhar from the village\" data-name-he=\"יששכר איש כפר ברקאי\" data-crossline-group=\"name-ref-crossline-58648\">אִישׁ כְּפַר בַּרְקַאי</span> לְמִיטְרַפְסֵיהּ מִינֵּיהּ בְּהַאי עָלְמָא. <span class=\"sentence\" id=\"1\" type=\"start\">&star;</span>אָמַר <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Rav Ashi, sixth-generation Amora\" data-authority-id=\"571\" data-full-name=\"Rav Ashi\" data-name-he=\"רב אשי\">רַב אָשֵׁי</span>: <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-tanna\" data-sage-type=\"tanna\" title=\"Yissakhar from the village, first-generation Tanna\" data-authority-id=\"1998\" data-full-name=\"Yissakhar from the village\" data-name-he=\"יששכר איש כפר ברקאי\" data-crossline-group=\"name-ref-crossline-58650\">יִשָּׂשׂכָר</span>",
      "segment_ids": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "0px",
      "width": "655px",
      "text": "<span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-tanna\" data-sage-type=\"tanna\" title=\"Yissakhar from the village, first-generation Tanna\" data-authority-id=\"1998\" data-full-name=\"Yissakhar from the village\" data-name-he=\"יששכר איש כפר ברקאי\" data-crossline-group=\"name-ref-crossline-58650\">אִישׁ כְּפַר בַּרְקַאי</span> לָא תְּנָא מַתְנִיתִין. דִּתְנַן, <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-tanna\" data-sage-type=\"tanna\" title=\"Rabbi Shimon ben Yoḥai, fifth-generation Tanna\" data-authority-id=\"2830\" data-full-name=\"Rabbi Shimon ben Yoḥai\" data-name-he=\"רבי שמעון בן יוחאי\">רַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן</span> אוֹמֵר: כְּבָשִׂים קוֹדְמִים",
      "segment_ids": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "0px",
      "width": "655px",
      "text": "לָעִזִּים בְּכׇל מָקוֹם, יָכוֹל מִפְּנֵי שֶׁמּוּבְחָרִין בְּמִינָן — תַּלְמוּד לוֹמַר: ״אִם כֶּבֶשׂ יָבִיא",
      "segment_ids": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "0px",
      "width": "655px",
      "text": "קׇרְבָּנוֹ״, מְלַמֵּד שֶׁשְּׁנֵיהֶן שְׁקוּלִין כְּאֶחָד. <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Ravina II, sixth and seventh-generation Amora\" data-authority-id=\"2647\" data-full-name=\"Ravina II\" data-name-he=\"רָבִינָא ב׳\" data-resolution-rule=\"ravina_after_rav_ashi_in_same_sugya\" data-resolution-explanation=\"Resolved to Ravina II because Rav Ashi appears earlier in the same sugya.\" data-resolution-reasons=\"[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;heuristic&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Ravina after rav ashi in same sugya&quot;,&quot;detail&quot;:&quot;Resolved to Ravina II because Rav Ashi appears earlier in the same sugya.&quot;,&quot;attribution&quot;:&quot;Girsology disambiguation heuristics&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;scholarly_source&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Iggeret Rav Sherira Gaon witness&quot;,&quot;detail&quot;:&quot;Iggeret Rav Sherira Gaon treats Ravina as the close of hora&#x27;ah, including the tradition &#x27;Rav Ashi and Ravina, end of הוראה&#x27;.&quot;,&quot;attribution&quot;:&quot;Epistle of Rav Sherira Gaon 1:81&quot;,&quot;citations&quot;:[&quot;Epistle of Rav Sherira Gaon 1:81&quot;,&quot;Epistle of Rav Sherira Gaon 1:108&quot;,&quot;Epistle of Rav Sherira Gaon 1:108&quot;]}]\">רָבִינָא</span> אָמַר: אֲפִילּוּ מִקְרָא נָמֵי לָא",
      "segment_ids": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "0px",
      "width": "655px",
      "text": "קְרָא, דִּכְתִיב: ״אִם כֶּבֶשׂ״, ״אִם עֵז״, אִי בָּעֵי כֶּבֶשׂ — לַיְיתֵיהּ, אִי בָּעֵי עֵז — לַיְיתֵיהּ<span class=\"sugya-marker sugya-marker-vilna-piska\" data-sugya-kind=\"vilna-piska\" data-sugya-id=\"210\" data-raw-symbol=\"׃\">׃</span> <span class=\"sentence\" id=\"2\" type=\"start\">&star;</span><br><br><big><strong>הַדְרָן עֲלָךְ מָקוֹם שֶׁנָּהֲגוּ וּסְלִיקָא לַהּ פֶּסַח רִאשׁוֹן<br><br></strong></big>",
      "segment_ids": [
        2
      ]
    }
  ],
